# Structify AI development (mandatory)

Full text (SSOT): [docs/AI开发规范.md](docs/AI开发规范.md). Also follow [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md).

## Hard rules

- Model proposes teaching text; **server** binds resources, budgets, permissions, authoritative state, and publication.
- Generation must not publish; publication must not call a model. Model output cannot authorize resources, change run identity, or reset budgets.
- Target flow only: reviewed outline → frozen fragments → bounded preparation → validated publication → knowledge-point navigation. Do not revive UNIT chain or dual generation modes.
- Preserve draft revisions, run fencing, leases, idempotency, and token accounting.
- New product workflows go to Spring `/api/v1/*`. Do not add studyroom workflows to `backend/node`.
- SSOT: OpenAPI + fixtures for HTTP; Flyway for schema; `docs/architecture/studyroom.md` + `docs/adr/backend/` for agent behavior; `docs/architecture/backend-standards.md` for Spring layering/MyBatis.
- Do not claim tests passed or production fixed without running checks / evidence. `docs/archive/` is historical only.
- No paid real-model calls in ordinary unit/e2e. No secrets, `.env`, `private/`, or courseware in git. No `git add .`.
- Before studyroom changes: read studyroom architecture + relevant ADR. After changes: run `node scripts/verify-studyroom.mjs --scope <needed>`; never report unimplemented scopes as success.
